# Set to "true" to simulate Zoho Creator submissions locally.
# Set to "false" for real submissions through the Creator Widget SDK v2.
VITE_USE_CREATOR_MOCK=true

# Creator application link name (SDK v2). Defaults to external-deal-response.
# VITE_CREATOR_APP_NAME=external-deal-response

# Optional overrides (defaults shown).
# VITE_CREATOR_FORM_LINK_NAME=Deal_Response_Form
# VITE_CREATOR_REPORT_LINK_NAME=All_Responses

# Publish keys ("private links") for external / anonymous users.
# Set BOTH to make the widget use ZOHO.CREATOR.PUBLISH calls.
# Leave both unset to use ZOHO.CREATOR.DATA and FILE calls (logged-in Creator users).
# The key is the last path segment of the published form / report URL.
# VITE_CREATOR_FORM_PRIVATE_LINK=
# VITE_CREATOR_REPORT_PRIVATE_LINK=

# Every setting above also works WITHOUT the VITE_ prefix (USE_CREATOR_MOCK,
# CREATOR_APP_NAME, CREATOR_FORM_LINK_NAME, CREATOR_REPORT_LINK_NAME,
# CREATOR_FORM_PRIVATE_LINK, CREATOR_REPORT_PRIVATE_LINK). Vite hides
# unprefixed variables from client code, so vite.config.ts inlines them at
# build time. Useful on hosts that warn about the public VITE_ prefix.
# The VITE_ spelling wins when both are set.
